findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors including
    parse/permission failures. The config tests check loading behavior but none test
    that parse errors or permission errors are distinguished from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests in error_exit_codes.rs checking that Error Display
    doesn't leak server internals. However, the reviewer did not flag that eprintln!
    in main.rs still prints Display directly to stderr, so the mitigation is partial.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-113 CRLF header injection tests in siem_client.rs. Dev implemented
    CRLF rejection in client.rs:20-33. However, tenant_id still uses raw String rather
    than TenantId from axiathon-core, so the type-safety aspect was not caught.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but not the workspace
    dependency pattern violation.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''ConfigToml struct uses #[derive(Deserialize)]
    without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. A user who typos api_ur instead of api_url
    will get the default value silently with no warning.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert! with
    is_none() || ...). TEA wrote config tests but this specific assertion anti-pattern
    was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via let _ = config. TEA wrote config tests but did not flag this pattern.
